/* phiOS — Librewolf accent injection (S-41, master plan §6.7 target group
 * 4: "Librewolf: userChrome.css + preferenza chiaro/scuro. Iniezione
 * accento, classe C"). NOT WIRED into design/adapters.txt yet — see that
 * file's own comment on why: Librewolf/Firefox profile directories are
 * named with a random 8-character prefix generated at first launch
 * (<random>.default-release), not a fixed path phi theme set's plain
 * template-to-destination mechanism can target. This file is real content,
 * ready to be copied once a destination-resolution step exists (reading
 * ~/.librewolf/profiles.ini's own Path= key after first launch, which IS
 * deterministic on a given machine from then on) — that step is not built.
 *
 * Scope kept deliberately narrow ("iniezione accento", not a full re-skin):
 * the accent colour on the two chrome surfaces every session actually
 * looks at — the selected tab and the URL bar's focus ring. Custom
 * property names below (--tab-selected-bgcolor, --toolbar-field-focus-
 * border-color) are Firefox's own documented chrome theming hooks, but
 * this has never rendered in a real browser from this session — flagged
 * for cheap veto against a real Librewolf window.
 *
 * The light/dark preference itself does not need a line here: Librewolf,
 * like any GTK app, follows the portal preference phi theme set already
 * writes (internal/theme/set.go's setPortalPreference) — this file is only
 * the accent on top of whichever base Librewolf already picked.
 */

:root {
  --tab-selected-bgcolor: ${PHI_ACCENT} !important;
  --toolbar-field-focus-border-color: ${PHI_ACCENT} !important;
}
